      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-03-30_WidnesExaminer_art0013" n="art0013">
        <head>EXAMINER, FRIDAY, MARCH 30 1900 THE FREE CHURGH.ES.</head>
        <p>THE EXAMINER, FRIDAY, MARCH 30 1900 THE FREE CHURGH.ES.</p>
        <p>WILL DELIVER FREE AT YOUR DOOR,</p>
        <p>Thisandsome,ryich-toned Piano onlreceipt of 10/63 The first monthly payment, and guarantee it for 25 years. Discount for Cash.</p>
        <p>Phot3 Catalogues sent free to an;</p>
        <p>ieaders of The Warrington. Examiner,</p>
        <p>Organs and Harmoniums, 5/- per month.</p>
        <p>The meetings of the National Free Church Council at Sheffield are the obvious and proper subject for our notes this/month. The gather- ings were undoubtedly a conspicuous success. About 1000 representatives of Free Church Councils all over the country gathered in the cutlery city. They were exemplary in their de- votion to business. The general public also showed great interest in the proceedings. The galleries were crowded during the greater pare of the sessions. The sermons, addresses, and speeches were, without exception, good, very practical for the most part, and directly bearing on the work of Free Church Councils</p>
