      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-03-30_WidnesExaminer_art0024" n="art0024">
        <head>DRINK v. CONSUMPTION.</head>
        <p>DRINK v. CONSUMPTION.</p>
        <p>Which Causes the Most Deaths.</p>
        <p>14We are not able to say at the moment which of these two great curses causes the largest mortality, but the fact remains that but for these two scourges the Death Rate would be a great deal lower than it is. We know the cause of Consumption in a great many cases is heriditary, but in a many of these cases the disease could be prevented from taking a hold on the system by taking care. For instance, say a person who is consi- dered to be consumptive takes a chill, if that is not at once cured a cold will follow, and thus open the door to the germs of Consumption and Death. When you catch cold or take a chill take as soon as possible a dose of that deservedly world famed medicine, Levens Lung Linctus, and you will find that the chill passes off quite harml-ssly, and that the cold is cured. It is the finest throat medicine extant, and will at once cure that droaeful Tickling in the Tbroat,Bronchi tis, Asthma, Sore Throat, etc. Think how many deaths occur as the result of a com- mon little cold, and gnard against an early death. All the local Chemists, Co-operative Stores, and Patent Medicine Vendor- sell Lavans Lung Linctus, at is. lid., 2;. 91., and 4s. 61., or the proprietors, Green and Co., Chemists, Bolton, will send a bottle, post free, for those prices.</p>
