        <p>order. I was also troubled with that most painful complaint gravel, and passed several small ',tones, which caused me great agony. I lost a grem.t deal of flesh ; I formerly weighed as much as eighteen stone, and came down to about thirteen stone. and suffered very much from a pain in my be&amp; and was not able to work tor 15 minths, my sigut and bearing were also affected. "For seven weeks I was in the Sunderland Infir- mary, where they treated me for Sugar Diabetes, and afterwards as an out-patient at Snerburn Hospital. Not getting any better. I went to London, and was an in-patient at Guy's Hesoital, for three weeks, but, as I was getting weaker, returned home. " Hearing of Dodd's Kidney Pills, I got a box, and commenced to feel better at once. The shooting pains, especially in the lower limbs, commenced to leave me, and when I had taken the Pills for a few weeks, my neighbours began to thiek Um': I was going te recover, whereas six weeks before, they, as sve,l as myself, thouget I had not muh longer to live. I have continued to gain strength daily, and feel very thankful that I heard of Dodd's Kidney Pills, as I had given myself up as beyend recovery, and the doctors said it was of no use to give tee medicine, as they considered my disease incurable. I am pleased to say that through Dodd', Kidney Pills I now feel that life is worth living, as lam able to walk and sleep better ; have less thirst, my sight and hearing are very much better, and I feel in every way improved. I believe there are many people who, if they knew the good Dodd's Kidney Pills have done me, would be induced to try them to their benefit."</p>
