        <p>No less th3n 418 competitors ard eutitied to shsre the £lO consola!ion p-ize. Competitors who gave eight correct re- sults in this competition, can. if they prefer it, send six full coupons in the next competition indtsad of hiving their share of the prize seat on. THE COUPON PRIZE. The £3 coupon prize goes to Mr N ktnsell, Hagley, Bt., Halesowea, nett' tarminghaa., for 6260 coupons. THE AGGREGATE PFOZE.</p>
        <p>Mr. Arthur has scored 41 poiats :or the A vf.r,rAgate Prize ; Mr Zaple, 38 ; Mr Pco,ltor. 31; Mr :land. 3.; ; Mr Pittana (11./1.) 26; Mr Hutching,, 18 ; Messrs Caen, and Pittam (M.), 14 each ; Mr Chaplin, 13 ; Mc+rsts Ttigwell and Salt, 12 each ; Messrs Mason and Cook, 11 each ; several others are cloa a behind. 147iTSTIO. COMP° UND TrEete Mr.rk of Compound Essence for Co sighs an.i Colds,—Acivt• eLlckle o UffdLiaeTcHARTIC UM PILLS, digestive, correc- tive, and agreeably aperient, Sld., 131 d. Of all Chemsts. Advt, NEW SPBLNG TA.CKETS, Capes, Macintoshes and Im- perial Cloaks. Choice ass °I talent ot Vhite ailor Hats. Just receive.l.—W. T. WlLLit..ms, 71, Sankey-street, Warrington. PUBLIC BIiNBFIT TINDER THE CLOCK OR BEST 001 S IN LANCASHIlifi.—Adrt.</p>
