      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1900-03-30_WidnesExaminer_art0136" n="art0136">
        <head>EXANIIN ER, FRP AY. MARCH 30. 1900.</head>
        <p>THE EXANIIN ER, FRP AY. MARCH 30. 1900.</p>
        <p>with a blanket each, so I put my overcoat underneath a kit ba.,.; ir [mini?, with an air cu,hion. We sleep in clothes, and get up at 5.30. Th‘,.re is a swimming bath beonging 1-o thc club. A Lit of us went yesterday and w&lt;tlicio.. Two days tic.fore we had a bathe in a pool ,e 4 inches deep ; we lay down and rolled in the mud. Camp lite a rough gtub suits me well. It is fairly hot here, but nothing like Rangoon. It is hot when we turn in, but often becomes very cold before morning. It is grand country. Table Mountain is on one side of the camp and very high mountains on the other, but a long way off, with sandy rough ground be- tween. The dust is awtul, and we get absolutely black after every drill. We have found scorpions in the tent every day. We are going to get a tent dog ; there are a lot about. I got rather a nice pointer this morning,but it disappeared in a few minutes. I am afraid I cannot possibly get to Wynberg, but will if I can to see Chap- pell. The 21st troop are leaving for Naauwpoort to-day and we are going on Toursday, as we have now got all our horses. We went down this morning to fetch the balance from the Afric. We do not take our kit bags, only saddle wallets and haversack. I mnst turn in now as I am awfully tired and have to do stables at 5 a.m. to-morrow.</p>
        <p>Hetlth invitim; th's Council to appßint deleczates to at- ter' tie. will be hAi in Aberdeen front the 2nd to the 7th ot Augmt,l9oo. It was resolved that thie, Coulmitte, cannot Rea the.ir way to mom:mead the a)unzil to apty,iut Jelegatei. The (Jairrni hove.i the adoption of the minutes, which were are ti to. OVELISEERS.</p>
        <p>On the proposition of Str. Gilmour, seconded by Mr. Or:nand, the todowing centlemen were appointed over- seers : M.ssrs. JAin Simpson, John Sankey, Dr. J M Patterson and William Beatty.</p>
        <p>I:Ai was all tlm business. EARLESTOWN CRICKET CLUB.</p>
